# Git hooks are executed by sh. On Windows a CRLF line ending breaks the
# shebang line, so the hook fails with a "bad interpreter" error rather than
# running. Pin them to LF regardless of core.autocrlf.
#
# Deliberately scoped to hooks/ only: a repository-wide "* text=auto" would
# renormalize every tracked file and produce an enormous unrelated diff.
hooks/* text eol=lf
